## Unloaded/loaded standalone loop with a stderr diagnostic (not committed)
240 runs of --scenario remote/isolation --case happy, 6 parallel, pinned to cores 124-125 with
8 nice -n 10 busy loops: 0 failures (the window is a few microseconds per run).

## Root cause, proven by widening the window (diagnostic patch, not committed)
conformance/src/fixture/machines/remote.rs::link (origin/integration 070871b) read the wall clock into
Context.now, then minted the op id with uuid::Uuid::now_v7() from the live clock. Admission
(crates/ovis-terminal-core/src/ops/admission.rs:93 "if request.minted_at > self.context.now { return
Err(OperationError::InvalidParams) }") refuses an id minted after its clock. Whenever a millisecond tick
fell between the two reads, accept() failed InvalidParams, which internal() mapped to
{"kind":"internal","hint":"inspect the fixture's stderr"} while dropping the cause.
Diagnostic patch: internal() eprintln!s its argument; a 2 ms busy wait between the clock read and the mint.
Result: 3/3 runs fail at step 8 with the byte-identical reply of all three occurrences:
  failure={"detail":"expectation reply[child-on-bravo]/error did not hold","hint":"compare expected and actual values in the evidence","kind":"assertion_failed","step":"8"}
  first failed assertion={"actual":{"code":-32603,"data":{"hint":"inspect the fixture's stderr","kind":"internal","retryable":false},"message":"operation failed"},"check":"reply[child-on-bravo]/error","expected":{"$present":false},"passed":false}
  fixture stderr="F2A-DIAG internal: InvalidParams\n"
So: no isolation property was violated; the scenario's expectation is right; the harness's stand-in
for a remote launch minted its own operation inconsistently with the ledger's admission contract.
